WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.549 --> 00:00:04.550
How metal was that Eddie Munson moment in
the "Stranger Things" Season 4 finale?!

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.849
And why was it the perfect choice for the
character?

00:00:06.849 --> 00:00:08.580
Keep watching as we break it all down.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.790
"Stranger Things" fans have had a painstakingly
long wait for the final feature-length episodes

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:19.080
of Season 4, after Volume 1 arrived on May
27, but Netflix has finally released the last

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.689
two chapters, and they drastically change
the future of the hit series.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:27.179
While the end of Volume 1 revealed that the
terrifying villain, Vecna, is not only Henry

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:32.050
Creel but also One, Volume 2 mainly revolves
around the gang's attempt to kill him by using

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.200
Max as bait.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.379
After all, he's already had a taste of her
pain and he wants to finish the job.

00:00:37.379 --> 00:00:41.679
This is partly because Vecna's master plan
involves ripping open four gates across Hawkins

00:00:41.679 --> 00:00:45.320
using four deaths as a way of bridging the
real world with the Upside Down.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.400
The stakes have never been higher, and there's
been talk of a tragic death in the series

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.480
since before this season started.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.640
So it's a little nerve-racking when Steve,
Nancy, and Robin all lie in wait for Vecna

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.120
at the Creel house while Dustin and Eddie
keep the Demobats [DEM-oh-bats] distracted

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.930
with an impromptu metal concert at the trailer
park.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.210
Unfortunately, the battle comes at a high
price for Eddie.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.390
The leader of the Hellfire Club has been a
big focus this season since the Hawkins townsfolk

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.820
think he's responsible for the deaths of Chrissy,
Fred, and Patrick.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.720
It's all down to the (very real) satanic panic
that gripped the United States in the 1980s,

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.360
which led many to believe that Dungeons &amp; Dragons
was part of some sinister evil plot to corrupt

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.360
young people.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.500
"These murders are ritualistic sacrifices!"

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.390
Although Eddie spends most of his time hiding
and going on the run, he armors up to help

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.450
Steve, Nancy, Robin, and Dustin in the Upside
Down.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.340
Eddie's idea of distracting the Demobats is
a pretty inspired one — he grabs the Upside

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.280
Down version of his electric guitar and climbs
on top of the trailer to absolutely shred

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.530
Metallica's "Master of Puppets" as a siren
song to draw the Demobats away from the Creel

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.530
house.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.310
It's an act that fits his character perfectly,
since he's a metalhead as well as a Dungeon

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.330
Master.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:56.290
It's a pretty appropriate song choice too,
since Vecna is also a master of the Upside

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.290
Down.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:00.480
The scene allows Eddie to let loose for a
few minutes after spending days hiding in

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.460
the woods by Lover's Lake — he just gets
lost in the music, knowing that it's helping

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.860
in the fight against Vecna.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.700
"Are you ready for the most metal concert
in the history of the world?"

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.250
Eddie's performance is another example of
how powerful music can be in the series.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.200
After all, Kate Bush's "Running Up That Hill"
is Max's hopeful anthem to pull herself out

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.860
of the Upside Down in Episode 4.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.571
But Eddie putting himself on the line shows
he's grown up a bit.

00:02:25.571 --> 00:02:28.860
Unfortunately, Eddie and Dustin's plan works
a little too well and they have to deal with

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.640
a huge swarm of Demobats that assault the
trailer, eventually breaking in through the

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.640
vents.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.880
The beasts are small, but they're vicious.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.450
Dustin climbs through the gate back into the
real world, but Eddie severs the makeshift

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.680
sheet rope so that he can't come back through
and get hurt.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.740
Obviously, this leaves Eddie trapped in the
Upside Down.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.460
It's a selfless act of heroism, and it proves
that Eddie isn't afraid to grow up and take

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.640
responsibility for his own actions.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.061
Although at first it looks like Eddie might
get away from the Demobats on a bike, one

00:02:55.061 --> 00:02:59.240
of them knocks it out from underneath him
— and he's suddenly swarmed by the monsters.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.751
Choosing to save Dustin while drawing the
Demobats away from his young sidekick and

00:03:02.751 --> 00:03:06.380
the Creel house proves that Eddie has grown
up since the start of the season — when

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.880
he jokes about being held back at high school
and refusing to conform with society.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.020
Although Dustin gets back through the gate
to find his friend, he's too late — and

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:19.350
in a heartbreaking goodbye, Eddie passes the
mantle of Dungeon Master on to him, noting

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.430
that he didn't run away this time.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.930
Fans have been worried about Eddie's fate
for a while, and this loss definitely hurts

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.210
considering how charismatic Joseph Quinn was
in the role.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.850
But at least it had meaning.

